[CENTER][SIZE="5"][B][GUIDE] How To Root and Unlock the Bootloader LG L4 II E440g (MT6575)[/B][/SIZE]

[B][SIZE="4"][COLOR="Red"]WARNING: THIS MODIFIES THE BOOTLOADER — READ EVERYTHING BEFORE STARTING[/COLOR][/SIZE][/B][/CENTER]

[CODE]#include <std_disclaimer.h>
/*
 * Your warranty is now void.
 *
 * I am not responsible for bricked devices, dead SD cards, lost IMEI,
 * or any other damage. Back up everything and verify every hash before
 * flashing. YOU are choosing to make these modifications.
 */[/CODE]

[SIZE="4"][B]About[/B][/SIZE]

The LG L4 II [B]E440g[/B] (codename [B]vee4ss[/B], MediaTek [B]MT6575[/B]) has a locked bootloader. Its LK checks the signature of the boot and recovery images, so an unsigned recovery (TWRP, CWM) stops with a [I]Security Error[/I].

This guide does two things:
[LIST=1]
[*][B]Root[/B] the stock ROM with KingRoot. It flashes nothing, so it works with the locked bootloader.
[*][B]Install a patched LK[/B]: [B]9 small patches[/B] that skip the signature checks on the boot and recovery paths. It is written from Android with dd, using the root from step 1.
[/LIST]

[B]What you get:[/B]
[LIST]
[*]Unsigned recovery images boot, for example [URL=""]TWRP 3.1.1-0.2 for the LG L4 II E440g[/URL].
[*][B]No data wipe:[/B] nothing in this guide erases userdata.
[*]Fully reversible: the stock LK is included in the kit and goes back the same way.
[*]Android keeps booting normally with the stock boot image.
[/LIST]

[SIZE="4"][B]Tested only on the E440g[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*][B]LG-E440g, firmware E44010a[/B] (V10a, Android 4.1.2 JZO54K): tested on real hardware.
[*][B]E440, E445, E465 and every other L4 II variant: NOT tested.[/B] They ship different LK binaries.
[/LIST]

[COLOR="Red"][B]Do not use this kit on any other model or firmware.[/B][/COLOR] Step 3 compares your LK's SHA-256 with the stock E440g one before anything is written; if it differs, stop. A wrong LK flash can hard-brick the phone.

[B]Not the L5 II method.[/B] The LG L5 II E450g has its own patch (same technique, different offsets): [URL="https://xdaforums.com/t/dev-lg-e450g-lk-uboot-patch-to-boot-unsigned-recovery-images.4791303/"][DEV][LG E450g] LK/uboot patch to boot unsigned recovery images[/URL]. Never flash one phone's LK on the other.

[SIZE="4"][B]Download[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*][URL=""]LG-E440g-Bootloader-Unlock.zip[/URL] - 336 KB | MD5: af0ea34cb2f52894268f59d3aec6f84c
[/LIST]

The kit contains the [B]patched LK[/B] ([I]lk/lk-patched-E440g.bin[/I]), the [B]stock E44010a LK[/B] to go back ([I]lk/lk-stock-E440g.bin[/I]), SHA256SUMS and a README.txt with the same steps. Unzip it and run every command below from its folder.

[CODE]79c7148274a19e1159a302462d0b7ee4ffbd5d764e8a8ca012aa59057b62251c  lk/lk-stock-E440g.bin
49427f704d95b09fac8b172e5d18cb83cdb26c612b578ffee364c5a8acee0c79  lk/lk-patched-E440g.bin[/CODE]

[SIZE="4"][B]Requirements[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*]LG E440g on firmware [B]E44010a[/B], battery at 50% or more.
[*]A PC with [B]adb[/B] ([URL="https://developer.android.com/tools/releases/platform-tools"]Android SDK Platform-Tools[/URL]) and the LG USB driver (Windows).
[*]On the phone: Developer options enabled (tap Build number 7 times) and [B]USB debugging ON[/B].
[*][B]KingRoot[/B] for the root step.
[/LIST]

[SIZE="4"][B]Step 1 — Root with KingRoot[/B][/SIZE]

Check that adb sees the phone and that it is the right model:
[CODE]adb devices
adb shell getprop ro.product.model          (LG-E440g)
adb shell getprop ro.product.device         (vee4ss)[/CODE]

Install KingRoot on the phone, run it and let it finish. Then verify the root from the PC:
[CODE]adb shell "su -c id"        (uid=0(root) gid=0(root))[/CODE]

The first time, KingUser asks on the phone screen whether to allow root for the ADB shell. Allow it, or every [I]su -c[/I] below fails.

[SIZE="4"][B]Step 2 — Back up the partitions unique to your phone (do not skip)[/B][/SIZE]

These hold your [B]IMEI, RF calibration, Bluetooth/Wi-Fi addresses and the modem NVRAM[/B]. A ROM install, a KDZ or a full wipe cannot recreate them. Back them up now, while everything works:
[CODE]adb shell "su -c 'dd if=/dev/block/mmcblk0 of=/sdcard/nvram.bin bs=4096 skip=3584 count=768'"
adb shell "su -c 'dd if=/dev/block/mmcblk0p2 of=/sdcard/sec_ro.img bs=4096'"
adb shell "su -c 'dd if=/dev/block/mmcblk0p3 of=/sdcard/persist_lg.img bs=4096'"
adb shell "su -c 'dd if=/dev/block/mmcblk0p4 of=/sdcard/persist.img bs=4096'"
adb pull /sdcard/nvram.bin
adb pull /sdcard/sec_ro.img
adb pull /sdcard/persist_lg.img
adb pull /sdcard/persist.img[/CODE]

Expected sizes: nvram 3 MB, sec_ro 5 MB, persist_lg 8 MB, persist 6 MB.

[COLOR="Red"][B]Two traps on this phone:[/B][/COLOR]
[LIST]
[*]Read nvram from [I]/dev/block/mmcblk0[/I] with the exact [I]skip/count[/I] above (taken from /proc/dumchar_info). [I]dd if=/dev/nvram[/I] without a count does [B]not[/B] stop at the end of the partition and fills your storage.
[*]Always use [I]adb pull[/I]. Redirecting [I]adb shell dd[/I] output to a file on the PC corrupts binary data.
[/LIST]

[COLOR="Red"][B]Never share these files. They contain your IMEI.[/B][/COLOR]

[SIZE="4"][B]Step 3 — Back up your LK and check it (do not skip)[/B][/SIZE]

[CODE]adb shell "su -c 'dd if=/dev/uboot of=/sdcard/lk-backup.bin bs=512 count=1024; chmod 644 /sdcard/lk-backup.bin'"
adb pull /sdcard/lk-backup.bin
sha256sum lk-backup.bin
(Windows: certutil -hashfile lk-backup.bin SHA256)[/CODE]

[LIST]
[*][B]79c7148274a19e1159a302462d0b7ee4ffbd5d764e8a8ca012aa59057b62251c[/B]: stock E44010a LK. Continue with Step 4.
[*][B]49427f704d95b09fac8b172e5d18cb83cdb26c612b578ffee364c5a8acee0c79[/B]: already patched. You are done.
[*][COLOR="Red"][B]Anything else: STOP.[/B][/COLOR] Your LK is different and this patch is not for it. Do not flash anything.
[/LIST]

[I]/dev/uboot[/I] is an MTK character device: read it with [I]bs=512 count=1024[/I] (524288 bytes). Without a count it does not stop at the end of the partition.

[SIZE="4"][B]Step 4 — Flash the patched LK[/B][/SIZE]

[CODE]adb push lk/lk-patched-E440g.bin /sdcard/lk-patched.bin
adb shell "su -c 'dd if=/sdcard/lk-patched.bin of=/dev/uboot; sync'"[/CODE]

[SIZE="4"][B]Step 5 — Verify the readback before rebooting[/B][/SIZE]

[I]sync[/I] and [I]drop_caches[/I] make sure the readback comes from the eMMC itself and not from what is still in memory: otherwise the check can pass while the partition is not completely written yet, and a reboot right away leaves it half written.

[CODE]adb shell "su -c 'sync; echo 3 > /proc/sys/vm/drop_caches; sleep 3; dd if=/dev/uboot of=/sdcard/lk-readback.bin bs=512 count=1024; chmod 644 /sdcard/lk-readback.bin'"
adb pull /sdcard/lk-readback.bin
sha256sum lk-readback.bin[/CODE]

It must be [B]49427f704d95b09fac8b172e5d18cb83cdb26c612b578ffee364c5a8acee0c79[/B]. [COLOR="Red"][B]If it does not match, do NOT reboot:[/B][/COLOR] repeat Step 4 and check again.

Then reboot. Android must boot normally:
[CODE]adb reboot[/CODE]

[SIZE="4"][B]Restore the stock LK[/B][/SIZE]

From Android with root:
[CODE]adb push lk/lk-stock-E440g.bin /sdcard/lk-stock.bin
adb shell "su -c 'dd if=/sdcard/lk-stock.bin of=/dev/uboot; sync'"[/CODE]
Verify the readback as in Step 5 (it must be 79c71482…), then reboot.

If you flash a KDZ later, check your LK again with Step 3 before installing a custom recovery.

[SIZE="4"][B]Next step: TWRP[/B][/SIZE]

Install a custom recovery: [URL=""][RECOVERY][UNOFFICIAL] TWRP 3.1.1-0.2 for LG L4 II E440g[/URL]. Then, if you want a custom ROM: [URL=""][L4 II][E440g][ROM][UNOFFICIAL][4.1.2] CyanogenMod 10[/URL].

[SIZE="4"][B]FAQ[/B][/SIZE]

[B]Does this wipe my data?[/B]
No. Root and the LK patch do not erase anything.

[B]Does it work on the E440, E445, E465 or the L5 II?[/B]
Not tested. Only the E440g was tested, and the other variants ship different LK binaries. Step 3 stops on any LK that is not byte-identical to the E44010a one. Do not force it.

[B]Is there fastboot?[/B]
No. This MTK phone has no fastboot; boot and recovery images are written with dd from a root shell.

[B]How do I enter recovery?[/B]
Use [I]adb reboot recovery[/I] from Android or from TWRP.

[B]A recovery shows "Security Error".[/B]
The patched LK is not installed. Boot Android and repeat Steps 4 and 5.

[SIZE="4"][B]Technical details[/B][/SIZE]

The LK verifies the boot and recovery images on four paths (boot, two alternate boot paths and recovery) plus a check after the image is read. The same function exists in the E450g LK, recompiled at other addresses; all offsets were found again for the E440g and cross-checked against the E450g patch that was already verified on hardware.

[TABLE]
[TR][TD][B]Patch[/B][/TD][TD][B]Offset[/B][/TD][TD][B]Original[/B][/TD][TD][B]Patched[/B][/TD][TD][B]Effect[/B][/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]P1[/TD][TD]0x161BC[/TD][TD]C0 F2 0A 82[/TD][TD]00 BF 00 BF[/TD][TD]NOP BLT.W, boot path, after verify_image1[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]P2[/TD][TD]0x161D4[/TD][TD]C0 F2 03 82[/TD][TD]00 BF 00 BF[/TD][TD]NOP BLT.W, boot path, after verify_image2[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]P3[/TD][TD]0x1633A[/TD][TD]C0 F2 46 81[/TD][TD]00 BF 00 BF[/TD][TD]NOP BLT.W, path A, first check[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]P4[/TD][TD]0x16350[/TD][TD]C0 F2 36 81[/TD][TD]00 BF 00 BF[/TD][TD]NOP BLT.W, path A, second check[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]P5[/TD][TD]0x1637A[/TD][TD]C0 F2 E5 80[/TD][TD]00 BF 00 BF[/TD][TD]NOP BLT.W, path B, first check[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]P6[/TD][TD]0x1638E[/TD][TD]C0 F2 2B 81[/TD][TD]00 BF 00 BF[/TD][TD]NOP BLT.W, path B, second check[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]P7[/TD][TD]0x16562[/TD][TD]46 DB[/TD][TD]00 BF[/TD][TD]NOP BLT.N, recovery path, after verify_image1[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]P8[/TD][TD]0x16576[/TD][TD]BF F6 0C AF[/TD][TD]FF F7 0C BF[/TD][TD]BGE.W to B.W, recovery path always succeeds[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]P9[/TD][TD]0x164E2[/TD][TD]06 F0 57 FC[/TD][TD]00 20 00 BF[/TD][TD]Post-read verification returns 0 (OK)[/TD][/TR]
[/TABLE]

seccfg is all zeros on this phone (MTK secure boot is not configured); LG's own signature check is the only one, and it is what the patch skips. The offline patch script, which only accepts the stock E44010a LK and checks the output hash, and the full analysis are in the repository: [URL="https://github.com/chijure-android-system-development/lg-e450g-lk-patch"]lg-e450g-lk-patch[/URL] (folder e440).

